                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Ok, I've got to admit that I struggled for ten long minutes in the first map - it's an awesome in-game level tutorial, but it just.. forgets to tell us which keys we're supposed to press xD\nSo we'll learn to jump with space, directional or WASD keys to move, and shoot with.. with.. ok, fuck, with the left mouse button.\nWell, you can navigate the main menu (i.e.: play, mute or quit xD) only with your keyboard and enter so I thought of a key for shooting too, and there's no remapping option but.. that's definitely ok.\nThe game's super indie, made by just two developers, but it really fits an awesome arcade style - starting from graphics and music, ending with an addictive gameplay that can look shallow just during the first five minutes!\nAnd the game is FAST. You're gonna literally run and breeze in a single screen through tons of monsters coming from everywhere, constantly swapping your fire weapons - from chainguns with a continuous fire (hold left mouse button) to shotguns that have wide but slower kind of work.\nAlong with the enemies of course, lots of new random ammo will constantly appear on platforms and walls, and you'll be able to perform double jumps, jumps on walls, jumps on the enemies' heads and so on!\nThe game has been programmed just to entertain and provide a casual, short but addictive experience to the player and it manages perfectly to fit this description - there are just few levels, but you'll find  yourself stick onto those and shoot the hell out of everything you can xD\nAnd even if the bosses are few, like the stages, there's even some chunk of customization: in fact, there's a small shop that you can enter through the levels and customize your experience by buying your favourite weapons through the game's coins (you can also alter your game's aspect through \"paintjobs\" xD).. basically, you're gonna make money by grinding in a funny way due to the fast, arcade-like gameplay and you'll buy your favourite weapons, that will then appear on the field.\nPlus, you're gonna have combos, a bar on the lower right side of the screen telling  you when the boss is gonna come over, you'll basically have always some ammo on the playing field and the game flows so fast and funnily that really manages to get its goal! The gun customization option is a definitive plus in my view, you can choose the best ones (since some guns like the energy rifle aren't really that great xD) and play the few levels (not easy at all by the way!) like you prefer! \nIf you're searching for a casual shooter with responsive controls and great mechanics, with an arcade flavour, this indie game's really worth your time and money! Just don't take it like only a 5 minutes game, it can be addictive! :)",
